{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4bb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a076ec-3023-7ad0-af14-c3080467cd16"},"sequence":184,"recorded_at":1780531400000363,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"29de407d-d987-4950-b9b4-211f15150d27","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"29de407d-d987-4950-b9b4-211f15150d27","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"29de407d-d987-4950-b9b4-211f15150d27"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"130f0eb8-5f89-47f6-aaad-3a3882c31913"},"task_id":"130f0eb8-5f89-47f6-aaad-3a3882c31913","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"130f0eb8-5f89-47f6-aaad-3a3882c31913","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-1i3qu7/worktree/internal/specdoc/SPEC.md`.\n(11213 line(s) above)\n11214|## 16. Security and threat boundary\n11215|\n11216|### 16.1 Trusted mesh model\n11217|\n11218|The security boundary is a trusted project mesh. Each authorized host and its\n11219|local operator can read synchronized project/session payloads. <code>ax</code>\n11220|does not protect payload confidentiality from an authorized peer, a trusted\n11221|provider plugin, or a compromised local user account.\n11222|\n11223|Peers MUST be explicitly allowlisted by stable host ID and SSH endpoint.\n11224|Tailscale discovery MAY propose hosts but MUST NOT authorize them. SSH protects\n11225|authentication, integrity, and confidentiality in transport. v0.5.0 provides no\n11226|default payload encryption at rest and MUST NOT claim otherwise.\n11227|\n11228|Machine-local credentials are a prerequisite at the destination. A successful\n11229|snapshot transfer MUST NOT imply that provider or remote-board authentication\n11230|will succeed.\n11231|\n11232|### 16.2 Mandatory exclusions\n11233|\n11234|No manifest or bundle generated by <code>ax</code> MAY intentionally include:\n11235|\n11236|| Class | Examples |\n11237|| --- | --- |\n11238|| Provider credentials | API keys, OAuth tokens, <code>auth.json</code>, account cookies, subscription tokens |\n11239|| SSH/private identity | SSH private keys, agent sockets, known-host mutation state |\n11240|| Environment secrets | Secret environment values, dotenv secrets unless explicitly managed as project content outside <code>ax</code> |\n11241|| Machine authentication | Apple Keychain, Secret Service, Windows Credential Manager, task-board login tokens |\n11242|| Live process identity | PIDs used for control, process handles, terminal IDs used as authority |\n11243|| IPC/runtime | Unix sockets, named pipes, tmux server sockets, session-message tokens |\n11244|| TerminalBackend runtime | Terminal Instance Bindings, backend native references/generations, attach endpoints/tokens, relay credentials, backend auth/private live databases, GUI/login attestations, terminal state/output/scrollback, process observations |\n11245|| Transient locking | Lock files, live SQLite WAL/SHM/journals, updater locks, provider PID locks |\n11246|| Mutable derived indexes | <code>ax</code> SQLite and provider caches not required by a documented import/resume contract |\n11247|\n11248|Opaque durable provider history MAY contain historical paths or historical PID\n11249|facts inside byte-preserved transcripts. Those facts MAY be transferred as\n11250|sensitive history when required for native resume, but MUST remain inert and\n11251|MUST NOT be treated as current process, ownership, or routing authority. This\n11252|does not permit copying a live PID/lock control artifact.\n11253|\n11254|The exclusions apply uniformly to every TerminalBackend. The tmux socket and\n11255|provider authentication state remain machine-local and MUST NOT be replicated.\n11256|The same rule covers ConPTY handles/named pipes and any future backend's local\n11257|IPC, attach/auth material, generation, live database, or mutable endpoint. This\n11258|applies even when an endpoint path is stable, an Aqua-started server survives a\n11259|terminal disconnect, or authentication works in the source server realm; none\n11260|of those facts makes runtime or credential state a transfer member. Section\n11261|11.9 permits only validated sanitized identity/conformance/capability evidence;\n11262|it does not permit reconstructing a Terminal Instance Binding.\n11263|\n11264|Transcripts and tool outputs can themselves contain secrets entered by an\n11265|operator or printed by tools. v0.5.0 does not claim reliable content-level\n11266|secret scrubbing. Operators MUST therefore treat all payloads as sensitive and\n11267|authorize only trusted project peers. An implementation SHOULD offer a\n11268|best-effort scanner and warning, but scanner success MUST NOT be described as a\n11269|confidentiality guarantee.\n11270|\n11271|### 16.3 Path and filesystem safety\n11272|\n11273|Receivers MUST treat manifests, filenames, symlinks, hardlinks, modes, provider\n11274|plans, and archive members as untrusted input even from an allowlisted peer.\n11275|They MUST prevent:\n11276|\n11277|- path traversal, absolute paths, drive/UNC injection, alternate streams, and\n11278|  repeatedly encoded separators;\n11279|- symlink/reparse escape during both validation and commit;\n11280|- case-fold collisions on case-insensitive destinations;\n11281|- replacement of unmanaged paths;\n11282|- device/FIFO/socket creation;\n11283|- broad deletion from tombstones; and\n11284|- time-of-check/time-of-use swaps by validating through directory handles or\n11285|  equivalent safe filesystem primitives.\n11286|\n11287|Archive extraction MUST occur inside a newly created staging root. Validation\n11288|MUST be repeated after extraction and before commit.\n11289|\n11290|### 16.4 Command and plugin safety\n11291|\n11292|All process invocations MUST use argv arrays and native process APIs. Shell\n11293|command construction from names, paths, provider output, or peer data is\n11294|forbidden. Remote SSH commands MUST use a fixed <code>ax</code> entry point and\n11295|platform-safe encoding.\n11296|\n11297|Provider plugins are privileged code. Explicit trust by path/digest is required\n11298|unless compiled in. Plugin stdout is protocol input and MUST be validated.\n11299|Plugin stderr, provider logs, and doctor output MUST be redacted before\n11300|persistence.\n11301|\n11302|TerminalBackend implementations and local-program adapters are independently\n11303|privileged. A built-in is selected only by its AX-shipped identity; an external\n11304|executable requires the closed Configuration 3 trust tuple and an exact\n11305|Manifest/Probe implementation digest. PATH lookup, basename trust, mutable\n11306|symlink substitution, duplicate discovery, manifest/probe disagreement, and\n11307|implementation drift fail before activation. Backend argv is fixed by the\n11308|registered adapter and every delegated provider entry point is exactly\n11309|<code>ax pane SESSION_ID</code>; configuration cannot supply a raw command,\n11310|arbitrary blob, secret, or unrestricted environment passthrough.\n11311|\n11312|For cloning, historical instructions/messages/tool output are untrusted data\n11313|and cannot select operations, paths, capabilities, or authority. The Session\n11314|Adapter receives only operation-specific read handles and fresh sinks, never\n11315|the AX object-store root or Provider rollback token. Credentials, auth stores,\n11316|cookies, keychain material, approval/trust caches, MCP credentials, secret\n11317|environment values, live process/PTY state, sockets, PIDs, locks, WAL/SHM,\n11318|rate-limit state, and account/server state MUST NOT enter a Clone Bundle.\n11319|\n11320|### 16.5 Force-takeover risk\n11321|\n11322|Epoch fencing protects converged <code>ax</code> state; it cannot stop an\n11323|unreachable old process from changing its local workspace or external systems.\n11324|Force takeover MUST therefore:\n11325|\n11326|- require explicit owner/epoch expectations;\n11327|- warn about split brain and external side effects;\n11328|- avoid overwriting either workspace history;\n11329|- preserve losing-lease events and both workspace checkpoints; and\n11330|- fence stale history from authoritative sync/resume after convergence.\n11331|\n11332|### 16.6 Out of scope\n11333|\n11334|v0.5.0 does not provide Byzantine consensus, hostile-peer isolation,\n11335|multi-tenant access control, end-to-end snapshot encryption, secret\n11336|distribution, provider-account migration, revocation of actions already sent\n11337|to external services, live-process cloning, task-board authority cloning, or\n11338|sandboxing stronger than the provider/OS configuration selected by the\n11339|operator. Clone does not add an N-by-N converter matrix or a second workspace\n11340|replication system.\n11341|\n11342|### 16.7 Directory, enrichment, query, and terminal safety\n11343|\n11344|Directory inputs include hostile transcript/tool text, repository/provider\n11345|names, paths, model output, peer records, query strings, and terminal text. No\n11346|content obtained from a session is an instruction to an adapter, worker,\n11347|planner, shell, terminal, or operator action. Synthetic prompts/checkpoints are\n11348|constructed from typed escaped fields; arbitrary summaries never select tools,\n11349|paths, schema tags, permissions, routes, or argv.\n11350|\n11351|Discovery reads only allowlisted adapter-declared native roots and explicitly\n11352|rejects credential/auth roots. Raw native IDs, transcript/preview bodies,\n11353|system/developer instructions, hidden/opaque reasoning, raw tools, attachments,\n11354|files, credentials, auth databases, environment values, model payloads,\n11355|terminal output, PIDs, PTYs, sockets, and absolute native-store paths are\n11356|excluded from directory replication, default indexing, plans, logs, and\n11357|metrics. Authentication is only the four-value status enum.\n11358|\n11359|Enrichment inputs are immutable, bounded, redacted public user/assistant\n11360|projections by default. The worker has no ambient filesystem, shell, network,\n11361|provider, Session, lease, workspace-write, terminal, or cloning authority.\n11362|Only an explicit Profile may grant one configured model channel; credentials\n11363|remain outside the Profile/request/receipt. Output validates the closed\n11364|annotation payload, size, evidence, head, and redaction policy before\n11365|publication and cannot set identity, ownership, capabilities, routes,\n11366|operator-only metadata, or executable arguments.\n11367|\n11368|Field authorization and redaction occur server-side before query serialization\n11369|or mesh publication; caller projection cannot widen authority. Preview and\n11370|transcript grep are source-local, explicit, and hard-bounded. Metadata policy\n11371|tightening prevents new sends but is not a remote deletion claim. Debug native-\n11372|file logging is off by default, local, bounded, owner-only, and requires a\n11373|redacted export manifest.\n11374|\n11375|All native/process launches use structured argv, explicit workspace-derived cwd,\n11376|minimal environment allowlists, safe-open/no-follow path handling, owner-only\n11377|staging, and existing cloning/provider transaction authorities. Provider IDs,\n11378|titles, paths, queries, and transcript fragments are never evaluated by a\n11379|shell. TUI and CLI rendering strips or visibly escapes ANSI/OSC sequences,\n11380|control characters, bidi overrides, invalid encodings, and hostile-width\n11381|graphemes before terminal output.\n11382|\n11383|Metric labels are bounded and never contain Session/instance IDs, transcript,\n11384|path, prompt, title, summary, or model input. Audit may contain plan/operation/\n11385|record IDs, actor, semantic intent, host/environment identities, policy\n11386|decision, state transition, and redacted error; it contains no content bodies,\n11387|prompts, credentials, terminal output, or raw environment values.\n11388|\n11389|## 17. Compatibility and migration\n11390|\n11391|### 17.1 Semantic-version rules\n11392|\n11393|Each contract in Section 1.5 versions independently:\n(more lines below)"}}}
