workspace checkpoints; and\n11330|- fence stale history from authoritative sync/resume after convergence.\n11331|\n11332|### 16.6 Out of scope\n11333|\n11334|v0.5.0 does not provide Byzantine consensus, hostile-peer isolation,\n11335|multi-tenant access control, end-to-end snapshot encryption, secret\n11336|distribution, provider-account migration, revocation of actions already sent\n11337|to external services, live-process cloning, task-board authority cloning, or\n11338|sandboxing stronger than the provider/OS configuration selected by the\n11339|operator. Clone does not add an N-by-N converter matrix or a second workspace\n11340|replication system.\n11341|\n11342|### 16.7 Directory, enrichment, query, and terminal safety\n11343|\n11344|Directory inputs include hostile transcript/tool text, repository/provider\n11345|names, paths, model output, peer records, query strings, and terminal text. No\n11346|content obtained from a session is an instruction to an adapter, worker,\n11347|planner, shell, terminal, or operator action. Synthetic prompts/checkpoints are\n11348|constructed from typed escaped fields; arbitrary summaries never select tools,\n11349|paths, schema tags, permissions, routes, or argv.\n11350|\n11351|Discovery reads only allowlisted adapter-declared native roots and explicitly\n11352|rejects credential/auth roots. Raw native IDs, transcript/preview bodies,\n11353|system/developer instructions, hidden/opaque reasoning, raw tools, attachments,\n11354|files, credentials, auth databases, environment values, model payloads,\n11355|terminal output, PIDs, PTYs, sockets, and absolute native-store paths are\n11356|excluded from directory replication, default indexing, plans, logs, and\n11357|metrics. Authentication is only the four-value status enum.\n11358|\n11359|Enrichment inputs are immutable, bounded, redacted public user/assistant\n11360|projections by default. The worker has no ambient filesystem, shell, network,\n11361|provider, Session, lease, workspa