{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4df","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a076ec-3023-7ad0-af14-c3080467cd16"},"sequence":202,"recorded_at":1780531400000399,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"29de407d-d987-4950-b9b4-211f15150d27","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"29de407d-d987-4950-b9b4-211f15150d27","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"29de407d-d987-4950-b9b4-211f15150d27"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"fa61b505-c296-4a98-8229-fbcab96cdc44"},"task_id":"fa61b505-c296-4a98-8229-fbcab96cdc44","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"fa61b505-c296-4a98-8229-fbcab96cdc44","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-1i3qu7/worktree/internal/specdoc/SPEC.md`.\n(11791 line(s) above)\n11792|## 19. <code>ax</code> implementation conformance and product release\n11793|\n11794|### 19.1 Implementation phases\n11795|\n11796|These are ordered phases for an implementation that intends to claim\n11797|<code>ax</code> product conformance version 0.5.0. They are not prerequisites\n11798|for publishing this specification and are not permission to ship a required\n11799|core target half-implemented:\n11800|\n11801|1. <strong>M0 — contract foundation</strong>: implement parsers, canonical\n11802|   identities, compatibility/error schemas, plugin wire contracts, internal\n11803|   plugin interfaces, the TerminalBackend registry/identity/semantic boundary,\n11804|   and the backend conformance harness. M0 MUST NOT advertise\n11805|   a public stable plugin SDK; that decision waits for Codex and Claude to\n11806|   validate the boundary in real implementations.\n11807|2. <strong>M1 — single-host durability</strong>: implement the derived index,\n11808|   direct plugin host, daemonless lifecycle, production built-in\n11809|   <code>ax.tmux</code> with its private dedicated server,\n11810|   stop/resume, workspace engine, and complete Git closure across tracked,\n11811|   dirty-index, staged, unstaged, untracked, ignored-policy, symlink, and\n11812|   submodule state.\n11813|3. <strong>M2 — multi-host MVP preview</strong>: implement SSH/RPC, immutable\n11814|   anti-entropy, resumable staging, workspace/provider/task-board transfer, and\n11815|   the minimum safety kernel: lease fencing, durable journal, idempotency,\n11816|   status-first recovery, and exhaustive crash-boundary classification. M2 is\n11817|   preview quality and is not the daily-driver gate.\n11818|4. <strong>M3 — first daily-driver tmux gate</strong>: pass the required macOS and\n11819|   Linux daily-driver lanes, including dedicated tmux/Aqua-broker functional\n11820|   evidence, complete graceful/force takeover recovery, destination readiness\n11821|   before ownership commit, and operator continuation UX with no implicit\n11822|   mutating route.\n11823|5. <strong>M4 — cloning, Directory, broader platforms, and release\n11824|   hardening</strong>: admit target writers only by exact tuple evidence; add\n11825|   local/mesh Directory and enrichment, managed continuation, and native\n11826|   Windows only behind their existing conformance lanes; then run the complete\n11827|   product-release acceptance matrix and migration/downgrade gates.\n11828|\n11829|Each phase MUST leave prior accepted fixtures green. Experimental provider cells\n11830|remain disabled and visible in doctor.\n11831|\n11832|### 19.2 Platform lanes\n11833|\n11834|The automated suite MUST provide these lanes:\n11835|\n11836|| Lane | Environment | Required coverage |\n11837|| --- | --- | --- |\n11838|| <code>PF-MAC-ARM64</code> | Current supported macOS on arm64 | Core CLI, split launchd/Aqua broker, dedicated <code>-S</code> tmux server, symlink/path-substitution refusal, sentinel plus provider-auth smoke bound to server generation/provider build/macOS version, logout/reboot parking, SSH loopback, Git/non-Git, local provider probes |\n11839|| <code>PF-MAC-AMD64</code> | Supported macOS on amd64 or reproducible hosted runner | Core CLI and providers that publish amd64 support |\n11840|| <code>PF-LINUX-AMD64</code> | Ubuntu 20.04+ baseline | Core CLI, systemd user, tmux, OpenSSH, filesystems, providers |\n11841|| <code>PF-LINUX-ARM64</code> | arm64 Linux | Core/storage/RPC and providers that publish arm64 support |\n11842|| <code>PF-WSL2-AMD64</code> | WSL2 with systemd and Windows-mounted plus Linux-home filesystems | Linux backend, tmux restore, path/locking/signal/auth differences |\n11843|| <code>PF-WIN11-AMD64</code> | Windows 11 24H2 PowerShell | Native ConPTY, Scheduled Task/service, OpenSSH, NTFS conflict/atomicity |\n11844|| <code>PF-WIN11-ARM64</code> | Windows 11 arm64 where provider artifact exists | Core CLI plus only documented provider artifacts |\n11845|\n11846|At least PF-MAC-ARM64, PF-LINUX-AMD64, PF-WSL2-AMD64, and PF-WIN11-AMD64 are\n11847|product-release-blocking core lanes. A missing hosted runner does not permit\n11848|claiming a cell; the project MUST use a self-hosted lane or leave it\n11849|conditional.\n11850|\n11851|### 19.3 Provider acceptance suites\n11852|\n11853|Suite codes:\n11854|\n11855|- <strong>D</strong>: probe, launch, identify, native stop/resume, persisted\n11856|  profile, native command interoperability;\n11857|- <strong>P</strong>: closed-store or backend-aware cross-host materialization,\n11858|  changed destination path, isolated Object Sink capture, per-blob resumable\n11859|  transfer, exclusions, prepare/status/commit/rollback recovery, validation,\n11860|  incompatible-version negative case;\n11861|- <strong>M</strong>: PTY/ConPTY input quiescence, idle proof, interruption,\n11862|  graceful exit, process/database flush;\n11863|- <strong>T1</strong>: task-board goal-bound primary launch/export/import/open/adopt;\n11864|  and\n11865|- <strong>TP</strong>: task-board tracked prompt launch/export/import/open/adopt,\n11866|  including a null-goal bundle.\n11867|\n11868|| Provider | macOS | Linux | WSL2 | Native Windows |\n11869|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n11870|| Codex | D, P, M, T1 | D, P, M, T1 | D, P, M, T1 | D, P, M, T1 only after native-store/ConPTY pass |\n11871|| Claude | D, P, M, T1 | D, P, M, T1 | D, P, M, T1 | D/P/M/T1 conditional pending native PowerShell/ConPTY pass |\n11872|| Gemini | D, P, M, TP | D, P, M, TP | D/P/M/TP conditional | D, P, M, TP on Windows 11 24H2+ |\n11873|| Muse | D on probed macOS tuple; P expected disabled; M conditional; TP | D/M/TP conditional; P disabled | D/M/TP conditional; P disabled | D/M unknown and disabled; P disabled; TP only if task-board runtime supports it |\n11874|| Antigravity | D backend-positive and backend-negative; P expected disabled; M | Same plus DBus/keyring | D/M conditional; P disabled | D/M conditional; P disabled |\n11875|| Pi | D, P, M | D/P/M conditional by exact version | D/P/M conditional | D/P/M conditional |\n11876|| Qwen | TP only | TP only | TP only where runtime probe passes | TP only where runtime probe passes |\n11877|| Future plugin | Negative unknown/disabled test | Same | Same | Same |\n11878|\n11879|For every C or ? cell, the suite MUST assert <code>enabled = false</code>,\n11880|operation refusal with exit 6, and an actionable doctor detail. For every U\n11881|cell, it MUST assert deterministic refusal and no provider/native-store\n11882|mutation. A capability MAY change to A only after its named suite passes on the\n11883|exact tuple and the evidence record is published.\n11884|\n11885|Muse promotion additionally requires subagent/tool-output/encrypted-reasoning\n11886|fidelity, benign cron fencing, clean exit, date-shard/path change, fork without\n11887|duplicated scheduled work, and incompatible-version failure. Antigravity\n11888|promotion requires same-realm success, different/no-account failure, deleted\n11889|backend UUID failure without blank replacement, cache merge preserving\n11890|unrelated entries, <code>Stop.fullyIdle</code> false/true cases, and closed\n11891|SQLite handles.\n11892|\n11893|Directory Version 1 requires the following for every exact declared Claude\n11894|Code and Codex tuple. Each claimed cell publishes machine-readable environment\n11895|and adapter build/provenance, OS version, fixture results, discovery/read-back\n11896|evidence, warnings, and conformance time. README prose is never capability\n11897|evidence.\n11898|\n11899|| Directory capability | Claude Code | Codex | Cross-host | Offline catalog |\n11900|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n11901|| Discover managed/unmanaged | Required | Required | Source node authoritative | Last converged view |\n11902|| Stable identity/head | Required | Required | Source node authoritative | Retained with freshness |\n11903|| Preview/redaction | Required | Required | Explicit source fetch | Unavailable unless source-local |\n11904|| Title/summary enrichment | Required | Required | Source-local job | Local subjects only |\n11905|| Same-environment continuation | Required | Required | Existing AX route required | Local-only eligible |\n11906|| Claude Code to Codex | Accepted source reader plus v0.3 clone evidence | Accepted target writer/read-back | Existing AX transfer required | Not remotely executable |\n11907|| Codex to Claude Code | Accepted target writer/read-back | Accepted source reader plus v0.3 clone evidence | Existing AX transfer required | Not remotely executable |\n11908|| TUI/query browsing | Required | Required | Required after RPC 3 negotiation | Required with stale/offline labels |\n11909|\n11910|Discovery does not authorize preview, adoption, native write, clone target, or\n11911|launch. Every such capability remains independently admitted for the exact\n11912|signed Environment Tuple under Section 13.14.5.\n11913|\n11914|### 19.4 End-to-end acceptance cases\n11915|\n11916|| ID | Required automated assertion |\n11917|| --- | --- |\n11918|| <code>AC-OWN-001</code> | One winning owner and zero/many replicas are derived from all union orders. |\n11919|| <code>AC-OWN-002</code> | Lower and losing same-epoch events cannot affect authoritative state and remain preserved. |\n11920|| <code>AC-LAUNCH-001</code> | Direct launch creates record/lease/wrapper/provider identity/checkpoint and native resume works outside <code>ax</code>. |\n11921|| <code>AC-LAUNCH-002</code> | Task-board public launch starts from a null creation-record manager ref, persists <code>task_board.launched</code>, survives a lost response with the same caller operation ID, exports an opaque bundle, and never reads private manager bytes. |\n11922|| <code>AC-PATH-001</code> | Flags, the exact five-variable environment registry, configuration loading, platform defaults, and every process component resolve identical roots; empty and unknown <code>AX_*</code> values follow Section 3.2. |\n11923|| <code>AC-TB-BOUNDARY-001</code> | Safe and unsafe bridge proofs map field-for-field into Checkpoint and RPC evidence; provider version/generation mismatch, background work, and a lost export response cannot publish a checkpoint or duplicate a bundle. |\n11924|| <code>AC-SYNC-001</code> | Set-union converges independent of peer/order/retry; live SQLite is absent from manifests. |\n11925|| <code>AC-SYNC-002</code> | 4 MiB chunk interruption resumes only missing chunks and validates the whole blob. |\n11926|| <code>AC-NS-001</code> | Every identity-bearing schema and raw blob maps to exactly one Section 11.4 namespace; excluded local objects change no root, and both independent implementations reproduce all <code>MIXED-NS-1</code> roots. |\n11927|| <code>AC-MAT-001</code> | Source-only provider capture writes only a fresh Object Sink; two blobs with chunk zero remain distinct; cross-host authority-scoped prepare/status/commit/rollback and every listed crash point preserve or restore exact bytes. |\n11928|| <code>AC-MAT-002</code> | Tagged workspace/provider/task-board/composite prepare/result fixtures preserve kind, intent, passive-versus-transfer cohorts, stopped-session behavior, and managed-replica nullability through status/finalize/rollback. |\n11929|| <code>AC-MAT-003</code> | Full Materialization Plan objects for all four kinds accept only their registered source/authority/action/validation/strategy combinations; provider and task-board one-root transactions have a legal strategy and every full negative object fails before staging. |\n11930|| <code>AC-MAT-004</code> | A lost <code>materialize.prepare</code> response is retried with the same caller-created operation/materialization IDs and canonical body, returns the byte-identical receipt after receiver restart, and creates exactly one journal and one set of derived authorities/IDs; a changed body fails with <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, while later status reads may evolve through durable phases under fresh request IDs. |\n11931|| <code>AC-PTX-001</code> | Fresh provider processes prepare/status/commit/rollback through the same host-created object/transaction authorities; same-filesystem and path-disjointness checks pass or fail before mutation, and all five rollback reasons round-trip exactly. |\n11932|| <code>AC-PTX-002</code> | <code>(operation, operation_id)</code> is the sole provider mutation idempotency key; a lost-response mutation retry that changes materialization ID, transaction ID, plan, authority, activation, or rollback reason returns <code>idempotency_mismatch</code> and creates no second transaction root; <code>materialize-status</code> carries no operation ID and may evolve from prepared to committed or rolled back. |\n11933|| <code>AC-MARKER-001</code> | Absent, matching, content/path-mismatching, replacement, and crash-reconstructed Managed Replica Markers produce the exact classifications, marker identity, atomic current/history writes, and fail-closed recovery in Section 10.6. |\n11934|| <code>AC-ATTACH-001</code> | Remote attach uses SSH, changes no lease/manifest, and reconnects after client loss. |\n11935|| <code>AC-TAKE-001</code> | Graceful takeover follows every phase, stops source before lease advance, persists profile, and leaves source a replica. |\n11936|| <code>AC-TAKE-002</code> | Failure before/after source stop and before/after lease advance has exactly the authority/recovery in Section 13.6. |\n11937|| <code>AC-FORCE-001</code> | Unreachable old owner is fenced after convergence; warnings/expectations are required; both histories survive. |\n11938|| <code>AC-FORCE-002</code> | Concurrent same-epoch force records select the same winner on every peer. |\n11939|| <code>AC-FORCE-DIRECT-001</code> | Direct force takeover stages before fencing, advances one lease, atomically materializes, proves the exact native/backend identity, and resumes without creating a blank session. |\n11940|| <code>AC-FORCE-DIRECT-002</code> | Direct capability/identity failure before fencing leaves authority unchanged; post-fence materialization/resume failure rolls back destination bytes but leaves the destination stopped owner. |\n11941|| <code>AC-FORCE-TB-001</code> | Task-board force takeover validates inert inputs, advances one lease, then prepares a journal/fresh staging root, commits import/open dormant, finalizes the exact adopt/resume binding, and never reads private manager state. |\n11942|| <code>AC-FORCE-TB-002</code> | Missing auth/bundle/bridge, expired tokens, lost adopt response, and post-adopt resume failure follow Section 13.7 without blank substitution or ownership rollback. |\n11943|| <code>AC-FORK-001</code> | Fork deterministically projects the old group/member/manifests to new identities, persists new topology/session/epoch-1 lease, runs direct or task-board materialization through prepare/commit/activation/finalize, and leaves every source object/authority unchanged. |\n11944|| <code>AC-FORK-002</code> | Failures before/after topology, session persistence, materialization, provider identity, bridge open/adopt, process activation, finalize, and event publication follow the Section 13.8 recovery matrix without blank identity or duplicate activation. |\n11945|| <code>AC-STOP-001</code> | Graceful stop creates checkpoint, closes provider, retains lease/state, and resumes with persisted profile. |\n11946|| <code>AC-BOOT-001</code> | Every epoch-1 pre-checkpoint direct/task-board launch failure is either idempotently retried under the same process/manager identity, promoted through a first checkpoint, or force-closed as a null-checkpoint non-resumable failed bootstrap; RPC/Event/CLI shapes agree. |\n11947|| <code>AC-RESUME-001</code> | No-materialization, workspace-only, provider-only, task-board-only, and both composite owner-resume paths execute their exact prepare/commit/activation/finalize or rollback/status recovery and emit one profile-consistent resumed event. |\n11948|| <code>AC-RESTORE-001</code> | tmux restore invokes wrapper and parks remote/stale owners; it does not migrate a session. |\n11949|| <code>AC-RESTORE-002</code> | Native Windows recreates ConPTY after reboot and resumes only after lease/checkpoint validation. |\n11950|| <code>AC-V043-REALM-001</code> | A background CLI/SSH/daemon may contact an existing attested Aqua broker but cannot create a credential-dependent tmux server; a narrowing mutant that permits Background creation fails through <code>terminal.ensure</code>. |\n11951|| <code>AC-V043-REALM-002</code> | <code>terminal.attest</code> rejects Aqua-only and sentinel-only evidence, requires a separate provider-auth smoke, and binds evidence to exact tmux server generation, provider build, and macOS version. |\n11952|| <code>AC-V043-ROUTE-001</code> | <code>ax NAME</code> auto-executes only one uniquely safe non-mutating attach/resume route; takeover, fork, move, and ambiguity remain pure plans requiring confirmation or return <code>interactive_choice_required</code>. |\n11953|| <code>AC-V043-SYNC-001</code> | <code>ax sync --all</code> converges immutable objects and policy-allowed projections without ownership change or runtime launch; an ownership-changing sync mutant is rejected. |\n11954|| <code>AC-V043-GIT-001</code> | <code>workspace.capture</code> proves tracked, dirty-index, staged, unstaged, untracked, ignored-policy, symlink, and submodule closure; independently omitting any class fails. |\n11955|| <code>AC-V043-TAKE-001</code> | Graceful <code>takeover.execute</code> proves destination broker/auth readiness, then verified source stop, ownership commit, and only then destination runtime creation; unsafe reordering fails. |\n11956|| <code>AC-V043-TAKE-002</code> | Force <code>takeover.execute</code> proves destination broker/auth readiness before persisting the force lease, never claims a verified source-process stop, creates a runtime only under the committed winning lease, and fences the prior owner from authoritative sync/resume. |\n11957|| <code>AC-V043-SEC-001</code> | <code>replication.select</code> excludes the dedicated tmux socket and provider auth state even when they are usable on the source; a socket/auth transfer member fails. |\n11958|| <code>AC-V043-SDK-001</code> | <code>release.admit</code> accepts M0 internal wire/interface/harness evidence and rejects a public stable SDK claim before Codex and Claude boundary validation. |\n11959|| <code>AC-CRASH-001</code> | Every applicable <code>CR-LAUNCH-*</code>, <code>CR-SYNC-*</code>, <code>CR-MAT-*</code>, <code>CR-GRACE-*</code>, <code>CR-FORCE-*</code>, <code>CR-FORK-*</code>, <code>CR-STOP-*</code>, <code>CR-RESUME-*</code>, and <code>CR-RESTORE-*</code> injection classifies into exactly one of <code>safe_retry</code>, <code>explicit_rollback</code>, or <code>recoverable_parked_state</code> with the Section 13.13 evidence record; no run produces duplicate live/authoritative owners, treats an unfenced external continuation as safe, or substitutes a fresh native provider/manager session for the persisted identity. |\n11960|| <code>AC-CLONE-001</code> | Every Capture Manifest candidate reconciles to included raw evidence or stable exclusion; every raw item reconciles to canonical evidence/disposition; every canonical item reconciles to staged/live target evidence or stable target disposition, including opaque events/reasoning, inert tools, stripped authority, and excluded credentials/live state. |\n11961|| <code>AC-CLONE-002</code> | Production <code>ax session clone run</code> rejects forged/self-minted, absent, stale, revoked, malformed, partially read, environment-only, or digest-drifted tuple evidence and rejects force bypass; a narrowing mutant that compares only environment ID fails. |\n11962|| <code>AC-CLONE-003</code> | G0-G1-A2 and G0-G4 positive chains validate; missing/skipped/forked/wrong-stage/forward/cyclic/byte-different successor chains fail through the production resolver. |\n11963|| <code>AC-CLONE-004</code> | Staged and live read-back, exact target identity, semantic markers, resume plan, Provider publication/finalization, target Checkpoint, events, receipt, and optional open use one transaction and never launch a blank replacement. |\n11964|| <code>AC-CLONE-005</code> | Every <code>CR-CLONE-01..16</code> boundary selects exactly one Section 13.13 outcome; rollback remains available through finalization intent and is forbidden after Provider commit; all bundle evidence survives. |\n11965|| <code>AC-CLONE-006</code> | Session Record/Event 2 fixtures prove a new target Session and immutable source provider ID; Provider-2 launch/fork rejects Session Record 2 and continues using exact Session Record 1 provenance. |\n11966|| <code>AC-CLONE-007</code> | The clone-only <code>creating -> stopped</code> edge accepts only the complete committed Provider/Checkpoint/no-process predicate and rejects origin/fork, missing/stale Checkpoint, rollback token, or process evidence. |\n11967|| <code>AC-CLONE-008</code> | Plan returns target G2 or archive A2 without live mutation; run rejects dry-run, archive flags are targetless, and CLI Result 2 preserves the target UUID versus record-digest distinction. |\n11968|| <code>AC-WORK-001</code> | The exact Section 10.4 Git root/child fixtures round-trip branch/detached HEAD, object pack, raw/logical index, staged versus working bytes, untracked files, modes, submodules, features, cwd, and project config without network access. |\n11969|| <code>AC-WORK-002</code> | The exact managed-tree variant round-trips and rejects Git-only members; concurrent capture mutation retries/fails. |\n11970|| <code>AC-WORK-003</code> | Divergent managed and unmanaged destinations fail closed; diff/copy/worktree/explicit managed replacement behave as specified. |\n11971|| <code>AC-WORK-004</code> | Shared checkout migrates as a group or separates into worktrees; one member cannot move alone while busy. |\n11972|| <code>AC-WORK-005</code> | Parent and every initialized submodule pack validate in isolated object databases; clean, staged-pointer, unstaged-pointer, and combined pointer triples round-trip without copying child objects into the parent pack. |\n11973|| <code>AC-GROUP-001</code> | Concurrent Session Record joins and authoritative session-Tombstone leaves derive one order-independent live membership set; conflicting topology records park the group. |\n11974|| <code>AC-GROUP-002</code> | Whole-group and separate-worktree fixtures revalidate the exact WorkspaceGroupExpectation at every phase and never silently shrink or partially activate a changed cohort. |\n11975|| <code>AC-TOMB-001</code> | All four Tombstone scopes and Acknowledgements validate; exact-path delete/modify/recreate golden cases converge or fail closed independent of union order; traversal/wildcard/root attempts fail; retention/ack/live-reference gates GC. |\n11976|| <code>AC-SEC-001</code> | Credential/key/socket/PID/lock/auth fixtures are excluded across direct and task-board paths. |\n11977|| <code>AC-SEC-002</code> | SSH/allowlist host-ID mismatch fails and discovery cannot authorize. |\n11978|| <code>AC-SEC-003</code> | Archive traversal, symlink escape, case collision, special file, and command injection fixtures fail. |\n11979|| <code>AC-TB-001</code> | Caller-ID launch/export/import/open is idempotent, open is dormant, only winning-owner adopt can resume, graceful/force stop are invocable, local board runs standalone <code>task-board validate</code>, and prompt bundles accept the conditional null goal. |\n11980|| <code>AC-TB-002</code> | Remote board transfers identity only and requires destination-local credentials. |\n11981|| <code>AC-TB-003</code> | Primary and prompt bundle projection preserves complete Board/Goal/Launch objects, non-secret literals, and extensions; the exact <code>sha256/HH/REST</code> archive member set rejects missing, extra, mis-sharded, and digest-mismatched bytes. |\n11982|| <code>AC-TB-004</code> | Durable task-board journal/status state recovers import/open/adopt/resume lost responses, crashes, expiry, and binding mismatch across graceful, force, passive, resume, and fork paths; bridge mutation never precedes journal creation. |\n11983|| <code>AC-PROFILE-001</code> | Direct and task-board start → profile change → checkpoint → takeover/resume/fork use one effective profile/source across bundle, plugin/bridge activation, and events; Pi's equal provider mapping does not erase the ax profile change. |\n11984|| <code>AC-PATH-002</code> | Every object, record, manifest, bundle blob, quarantine item, provider sink/source, and marker history maps a digest through the same two-hex-shard/62-hex-leaf algorithm on POSIX and native Windows. |\n11985|| <code>AC-VERS-001</code> | Contracts version independently; explicit containing-protocol Error bindings are honored; major mismatch/downgrade fail read-only and minor extensions preserve semantics. |\n11986|| <code>AC-ERR-001</code> | Every failure class returns the stable exit/error mapping and JSON stdout remains one document. |\n11987|| <code>AC-ERR-002</code> | Provider, bridge, and RPC compatible, incompatible-major, and pre-handshake/first-frame fixtures either use the statically bound Error 1.0.0 envelope or close and produce only the specified local error. |\n11988|| <code>AC-WIRE-001</code> | Every Section 1.5 contract and every embedded tagged variant in Appendix D accepts its positive fixture and rejects missing, null-invalid, enum-invalid, unsafe-number, oversized, forbidden-variant, and unknown members. Schema/path-directed common-type vectors reject non-prefixed invalid digests, malformed UUIDv4/UUIDv7, impossible calendar timestamps, and unsorted/duplicate nested arrays even after self-ID recomputation. |\n11989|| <code>AC-NUM-001</code> | Python, JavaScript, Go, and CBOR implementations agree on every Section 1.6 safe/decimal boundary vector; numeric 2^53 and wider values are rejected without rounding. |\n11990|| <code>AC-MERKLE-001</code> | Empty, singleton, branch, shared-prefix, and randomized ID sets produce the Section 11.4 roots in two independent implementations and every children response rehashes exactly. |\n11991|| <code>AC-CLI-001</code> | Every Section 14.3 non-interactive example parses; missing takeover destination, missing fork name/destination, action-inapplicable flags, and invalid materialize conflict flag combinations fail with their specified exits. |\n11992|| <code>AC-CLI-002</code> | Copy and worktree materialize the same session without lease change; managed replacement requires expected checkpoint, confirmation event, preserved divergence, and refuses unmanaged content. |\n11993|| <code>AC-CLI-003</code> | Goal-bound primary and tracked-prompt task-board launches require and normalize the exact board/mode/goal/binding inputs; local and explicit-peer log reads paginate with host-bound cursors and stable ordering. |\n11994|| <code>AC-CLI-004</code> | Local and SSH-remote log pages carry the actual non-null emitting host ID; cursor pages preserve it, and mismatched or forged remote results return no events. |\n11995|| <code>AC-DIR-INV-001</code> | Every <code>DIR-INV-01..45</code> assertion has a positive production-path fixture and a focused negative or narrowing mutation where rejection is required. |\n11996|| <code>AC-DIR-OBS-001</code> | Environment/Native/Batch self-IDs, source-host authority, exact-head derivation, root/realm absence proof, gap/branch visibility, and unchanged-history rescans obey Sections 2.2 and 10.8. |\n11997|| <code>AC-DIR-CAT-001</code> | Deleting local directory SQLite and rebuilding from immutable AX, cloning, directory records, and configuration reproduces the same entries, current heads, lineage, freshness, title resolution, and search results. |\n11998|| <code>AC-DIR-LIN-001</code> | Only registered authoritative evidence creates lineage; similarity remains a suggestion, weak identity blocks binding, and concurrent manual links remain explicit conflicts until a supersession DAG resolves them. |\n11999|| <code>AC-DIR-ENR-001</code> | Deterministic extraction works without a model; model input/output and worker authority obey the closed Profile/Job/Annotation contracts; exact-head and policy rechecks reject stale or over-authoritative publication. |\n12000|| <code>AC-DIR-QUERY-001</code> | CLI, TUI, and machine requests drive one typed query engine with exact projection, batching, cursor, preset, scoped-grep, authorization, redaction, and guarded-mutation behavior; agents never scrape TUI text. |\n12001|| <code>AC-DIR-PLAN-001</code> | Every route/outcome pair is closed; planning performs no mutation; execution rejects expiry or any changed expectation without silent replanning, route/fidelity substitution, or force escalation. |\n12002|| <code>AC-DIR-EXEC-001</code> | Adoption, managed resume/takeover/fork/clone/move, local unmanaged open, launch, attach, lost-response replay, and uncertain recovery enter through the real planner/executor and reuse AX/cloning authority without duplicate workspace, Provider, blob, or transaction state. |\n12003|| <code>AC-DIR-MOVE-001</code> | Cross-environment move validates and commits the target before source release; release failure preserves the target and reports <code>cloned_source_still_active</code>. |\n12004|| <code>AC-DIR-MESH-001</code> | RPC 2 and 3 interoperate only through dual-stack selection; RPC 3 advertises the exact 24 contract keys, has one disjoint <code>directory_record</code> namespace, verifies Merkle cardinality, and rejects unsupported peers without reinterpretation. |\n12005|| <code>AC-DIR-FACADE-001</code> | One environment implementation backs Provider 2, Session Adapter 1, and Directory Node 1/2; each negotiated major preserves its exact request vocabulary; contradictory tuple/parser/identity/redaction/capability claims fail closed and no façade becomes a second authority. |\n12006|| <code>AC-DIR-SEC-001</code> | Credential/auth roots, absolute native paths, raw transcripts/previews/tools/reasoning/attachments, terminal/process state, and secret canaries are absent from records, plans, bundles, indexes, logs, metrics, and peer results. |\n12007|| <code>AC-DIR-TERM-001</code> | Hostile ANSI/OSC/bidi/control/width strings render inertly, structured argv/cwd/environment launch admits no shell injection, and spawn alone never satisfies readiness. |\n12008|| <code>AC-OBS-001</code> | Required events/metrics exist and a secret/transcript canary never appears in logs. |\n12009|| <code>AC-DOC-001</code> | All internal section references, local links, JSON/TOML examples, tables, and traceability rows validate. |\n12010|| <code>AC-REF-001</code> | A schema-aware reference walker resolves every normative simple/dotted field expression and enum token against the containing closed registry (including MaterializationCohort fields), rejects aliases absent from that schema, and separately validates every extension key against Section 1.6. |\n12011|| <code>AC-DIAG-001</code> | Structurizr and all nine focused PlantUML sources render to fifteen committed SVGs; the fresh artifacts are visually inspected for clipping, width, contrast, readable labels, and arrow direction and match Sections 3–4, 10.8, 13, and 16.7. |\n12012|\n12013|### 19.5 <code>ax</code> implementation release acceptance rule\n12014|\n12015|An implementation MAY claim <code>ax</code> product conformance 0.5.0 only when:\n12016|\n12017|1. all product-release-blocking core platform lanes pass;\n12018|2. every A provider cell passes its suites;\n12019|3. every C/?/U cell passes its negative-advertisement tests;\n12020|4. all Section 19.4 cases pass;\n12021|5. no credential/excluded-state fixture enters an artifact;\n12022|6. its product documentation and generated examples validate from a clean\n12023|   implementation checkout; and\n12024|7. every Directory Node, record, query, planner/executor, RPC 3, CLI Result 3,\n12025|   Session Record/Event 3, Error 1.2, security, and all\n12026|   <code>DIR-INV-01..45</code> acceptance fixture passes; and\n12027|8. every TerminalBackend registry, identity, operation, capability, credential,\n12028|   compatibility, replication, CLI/Provider/Event/RPC/Error binding, tmux,\n12029|   ConPTY, and expected-red conformance case passes for each claimed backend and\n12030|   platform tuple.\n12031|\n12032|Unknown provider facts do not block an implementation release when, and only\n12033|when, their cells remain disabled and truthful.\n12034|\n12035|These runtime lanes and provider suites are an implementation-conformance gate,\n12036|not the <code>agent-session-manager-spec</code> publication gate. Section 20 MAY\n12037|publish the normative contract before any <code>ax</code> product binary exists;\n12038|it MUST NOT claim that the unimplemented runtime cases passed.\n12039|\n12040|## 20. Specification publication and governance\n12041|\n12042|### 20.1 Repository and release\n12043|\n12044|The specification repository MUST be public at\n12045|<code>relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec</code>, use <code>main</code> as\n12046|the default branch, and carry the MIT License. The current specification\n12047|release is <code>v0.5.0</code>. Existing release tags are immutable history and\n12048|MUST NOT be moved or rewritten. The v0.3.0 specification baseline remains the\n12049|normative cloning authority whether consumed from its release package or the\n12050|accepted baseline commit; this sentence does not claim that a particular tag\n12051|already exists.\n(more lines below)"}}}
