{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c503","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a076ec-3023-7ad0-af14-c3080467cd16"},"sequence":220,"recorded_at":1780531400000435,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"29de407d-d987-4950-b9b4-211f15150d27","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"29de407d-d987-4950-b9b4-211f15150d27","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"29de407d-d987-4950-b9b4-211f15150d27"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"2fefdb6c-c248-4edc-bf05-cce8e758a4bf"},"task_id":"2fefdb6c-c248-4edc-bf05-cce8e758a4bf","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"2fefdb6c-c248-4edc-bf05-cce8e758a4bf","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-1i3qu7/worktree/internal/specdoc/SPEC.md`.\n(12039 line(s) above)\n12040|## 20. Specification publication and governance\n12041|\n12042|### 20.1 Repository and release\n12043|\n12044|The specification repository MUST be public at\n12045|<code>relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec</code>, use <code>main</code> as\n12046|the default branch, and carry the MIT License. The current specification\n12047|release is <code>v0.5.0</code>. Existing release tags are immutable history and\n12048|MUST NOT be moved or rewritten. The v0.3.0 specification baseline remains the\n12049|normative cloning authority whether consumed from its release package or the\n12050|accepted baseline commit; this sentence does not claim that a particular tag\n12051|already exists.\n12052|\n12053|The release commit and annotated tag MUST both be signed using Ivan Oparin's\n12054|SSH signing key <code>~/.ssh/ivanopcode</code>. The commit author is:\n12055|\n12056|~~~text\n12057|Ivan Oparin <oparin@me.com>\n12058|~~~\n12059|\n12060|No AI <code>Co-Authored-By</code> trailer or other AI attribution trailer MUST\n12061|appear in any commit message, including the release commit. The release commit\n12062|MUST contain only the human author above and MUST be SSH-signed with\n12063|<code>~/.ssh/ivanopcode</code>. Automation MUST NOT stage, commit, tag, or push;\n12064|automation MUST stop before any <code>git add</code>/<code>git commit</code>/\n12065|<code>git tag</code>/<code>git push</code> operation and hand the exact reviewed\n12066|commands to the user for explicit human execution. The model MAY be acknowledged\n12067|only in prose documentation outside commit metadata, clearly marked as\n12068|non-commit attribution and only when explicitly requested; it MUST NOT appear as\n12069|a commit co-author.\n12070|\n12071|### 20.2 Publication gate\n12072|\n12073|This section governs the <code>agent-session-manager-spec</code> repository's\n12074|specification release <code>v0.5.0</code>, not an <code>ax</code> executable\n12075|release. The publication task MUST:\n12076|\n12077|1. verify a clean checkout contains SPEC, public operator/contributor guides,\n12078|   diagram sources and rendered SVGs, VERSION, CHANGELOG, release notes, and MIT\n12079|   License;\n12080|2. run the repository's accepted validation entry point as a standalone\n12081|   process and retain its real exit code;\n12082|3. explicitly verify that the publication validator does not require an\n12083|   <code>ax</code> binary, provider runtime, platform lane, or any Section 19\n12084|   product-conformance result;\n12085|4. verify <code>VERSION</code>, current document metadata, changelog, release\n12086|   notes, and the proposed tag all say <code>v0.5.0</code>, while every existing\n12087|   historical tag remains unchanged;\n12088|5. run the semantic crash/restart gate and its focused expected-red mutations;\n12089|   validation MUST emit an actionable diagnostic when the three-outcome\n12090|   exclusivity/exhaustiveness rule, boundary registry, evidence requirements,\n12091|   duplicate-owner prohibition, or exact-native-identity prohibition is\n12092|   weakened or removed;\n12093|6. prepare the exact signed-commit command with author\n12094|   <code>Ivan Oparin &lt;oparin@me.com&gt;</code> and no AI trailer, and hand it\n12095|   to the user for explicit review; automation MUST NOT stage or commit before\n12096|   human approval;\n12097|7. prepare the exact signed annotated <code>v0.5.0</code> tag command and hand it\n12098|   to the user for explicit review; automation MUST NOT create the tag before\n12099|   human approval;\n12100|8. after the human creates the commit and tag, verify both signatures locally\n12101|   with <code>git log --show-signature -1</code> and\n12102|   <code>git tag --verify v0.5.0</code>;\n12103|9. hand the exact <code>git push</code> commands for <code>main</code> and the\n12104|   <code>v0.5.0</code> tag to the user; automation MUST NOT push before explicit\n12105|   human approval and only after accepted validation/review;\n12106|10. verify the public repository, default branch, license, commit signature, tag\n12107|   signature, and release URL; and\n12108|11. attach publication evidence to the board.\n12109|\n12110|No automation MAY publish, stage, commit, tag, or push before validation\n12111|acceptance and explicit human review of every stage/commit/tag/push command.\n12112|Automation MUST stop before those operations and hand the exact reviewed\n12113|commands to the user. SemVer applies to specification releases; independent\n12114|schema/protocol versions remain as listed in Section 1.5.\n12115|\n12116|Publication acceptance case <code>SPEC-PUB-001</code> MUST run in a fixture\n12117|checkout containing no <code>ax</code> executable and pass all specification\n12118|structure, contract-fixture, link, diagram, metadata, and signature-preflight\n12119|checks available before signing. Any validator that tries to execute product\n12120|acceptance cases from Section 19 fails this publication case.\n12121|\n12122|Publication acceptance case <code>SPEC-PUB-CRASH-001</code> MUST prove that the\n12123|Section 13.13 outcome vocabulary is mutually exclusive and collectively\n12124|exhaustive, every boundary family and required evidence field is present, and\n12125|both duplicate-owner and silent-fresh-native-session recovery are forbidden.\n12126|At least one focused expected-red mutation MUST remove or weaken a gate clause\n12127|and MUST be rejected with a diagnostic that names the missing crash/restart\n12128|requirement rather than only reporting a generic document digest mismatch.\n12129|\n12130|## Appendix A. Normative traceability\n12131|\n12132|### A.1 Settled-decision traceability\n12133|\n12134|| Settled input section | Normative specification sections |\n12135|| --- | --- |\n12136|| Product and operator model | Sections 1, 2, 5, 13, 14 |\n12137|| Terminal persistence | Sections 3.1–3.2, 4, 13.4–13.13, 19.2–19.4 |\n12138|| Providers and native stores | Sections 7, 8, 13.1, 13.6–13.13, Appendix C |\n12139|| Task-board integration | Sections 2.2, 9, 13.2, 13.6–13.13, 19.3–19.4 |\n12140|| Mesh and replication | Sections 1.6, 3.2–3.3, 6, 10–12, 13.3, 13.13, 16, 19 |\n12141|| Attach, takeover, failure, and fork | Sections 5.3–5.7, 13, 14, 15, 16.5, 19.4 |\n12142|| Implementation stack and delivery | Sections 1.3–1.6, 3–7, 10–12, 17–20 |\n12143|| Publication metadata | Section 20 |\n12144|\n12145|### A.2 Story acceptance traceability\n12146|\n12147|| <code>STORY-260819-iscto1</code> criterion | Normative source and delivery route |\n12148|| --- | --- |\n12149|| SPEC.md is normative and detailed | This document, especially Sections 1–20 |\n12150|| README provides the operator interface | The repository README provides the entry point and contract map; Section 14 is the normative CLI/UX source, and downstream <code>TASK-260819-1i3olz</code> owns expanded public README/CONTRIBUTING rendering |\n12151|| C4 and PlantUML sources render successfully | Section 3.1 fixes C4 scope and Section 13 fixes sequence/state semantics; downstream <code>TASK-260819-37heok</code> owns sources/SVG/render evidence |\n12152|| macOS, Linux, WSL2, and native Windows PowerShell are explicit | Sections 3.2, 4, 8.4, 11.6, 13.11, and 19.2–19.3 |\n12153|| All settled decisions are traceable | Appendix A.1 |\n12154|| Independent reviewer accepts the artifact | Required board reviewer route after this task's <code>to-review</code> handoff |\n12155|\n12156|The Epic criterion for a signed public <code>v0.4.3</code> specification release\n12157|maps only to Section 20 and remains owned by the downstream validation and\n12158|publication tasks. Section 19 governs a future product implementation and is\n12159|not a prerequisite for that publication.\n12160|\n12161|### A.3 Task acceptance traceability\n12162|\n12163|| Task criterion | Normative sections |\n12164|| --- | --- |\n12165|| Exactly one owner, epoch fencing, replicas | Sections 2.2, 5.3, 11.4, 13.6–13.7, AC-OWN cases |\n12166|| Complete graceful/force/attach/fork/stop/resume preconditions, transitions, failures, recovery | Section 13, especially distinct direct/task-board force paths in 13.7, and Section 15 |\n12167|| Direct native-store and opaque task-board paths are distinct | Sections 2.1–2.2, 7–9, 13.1–13.2 |\n12168|| Union immutable replication; never live SQLite; conflicts fail closed | Sections 3.3, 10–12 |\n12169|| Manifests, staging, validation, atomicity, tombstones, workspace groups, Git/non-Git | Sections 10–12 and 19.4 |\n12170|| Honest platform/provider matrices including Windows/WSL2, Pi, Qwen | Sections 7.7 and 8 |\n12171|| Trusted mesh, allowlist, SSH, no encryption claim, machine-local credentials, exclusions | Sections 6, 11.1, and 16 |\n12172|| Independently versioned plugin/RPC/record/bundle/config/CLI result with explicit embedded-error bindings | Sections 1.5–1.6, 5, 7, 9–11, 14.2, 15.1, and 17 |\n12173|| CLI, exit codes, observability, implementation rollout/acceptance, specification publication | Sections 14, 15, 18, 19, and the independent Section 20 gate |\n12174|| No unresolved implementation question except provider version gates | Appendix B |\n12175|| Crash/restart classification has one exhaustive outcome and preserves owner/native identity | Sections 13.13, 19.4 <code>AC-CRASH-001</code>, 20.2 <code>SPEC-PUB-CRASH-001</code>, and Appendix A.8 |\n12176|| Approved v0.4.3 roadmap and macOS terminal-realm boundaries | Sections 2.2–2.3, 3.1–3.2, 4.2/4.4, 7.1, 12.1–12.3, 13.3/13.5–13.6/13.11/13.15, 14.1, 15.3, 16.2, 17.1, 19.1–19.4, and Appendix D |\n12177|\n12178|### A.4 Second-review closure traceability\n12179|\n12180|| Reviewer finding | Normative closure |\n12181|| --- | --- |\n12182|| Closed registry and embedded shapes | Sections 5.4–5.6, 7.5, 10.4, 18.1, and the exhaustive positive/negative fixture rules in Appendix D |\n12183|| Exact Git and managed-tree state | Section 10.4 tagged manifests, recursive submodule state, language-neutral pack/index/blob corpus, and Section 12 round-trip rules |\n12184|| Canonical state and destination enums | SessionState in Section 5.7, explicit task-board mapping in Section 9.2, DestinationClass in Sections 11.3 and 11.7, and their RPC/CLI reuse |\n12185|| Executable task-board creation and persistence | Public launch/idempotency/force-stop bridge in Section 9.2, nullable prompt bundle in Section 9.3, and launch/takeover flows in Section 13 |\n12186|| Provider capture, transfer, and rollback | Object Sink plus capture and prepare/status/commit/rollback in Section 7.5, per-blob journal state in Section 10.6, and composite recovery in Sections 11.3 and 13 |\n12187|| JCS integer interoperability | Safe JSON number domain, decimal-string escape hatch, and cross-language boundary vectors in Section 1.6 plus AC-NUM cases in Section 19.4 |\n12188|| Public conflict-resolution UX | Exact copy/worktree/managed-replacement grammar, confirmation policy, CLI Result, and accepted/rejected fixtures in Sections 14.1–14.3 |\n12189|\n12190|### A.5 Third-review closure traceability\n12191|\n12192|| Reviewer finding | Normative closure |\n12193|| --- | --- |\n12194|| Contradictory environment overrides | One five-entry flag/environment registry, value-kind and empty/unknown rules in Section 3.2; identical precedence in Sections 6.1 and 14.2; <code>AC-PATH-001</code> and Appendix D fixtures |\n12195|| Missing task-board safe-boundary facts | Closed <code>BridgeSafeBoundary</code>, provider-version result, safe/unsafe/lost-response fixtures, and total bridge-to-Checkpoint-to-RPC mapping in Sections 9.2, 11.3, 13.2, and 13.6 |\n12196|| Provider capture/materialization roots were unnamed | Disjoint capture/materialize request variants and source authorities in Section 7.5; destination <code>RootAuthority</code>, per-operation target/predecessor/boundary, and cross-host fixtures in Sections 10.5 and 11.6 |\n12197|| Managed-replica marker had no contract | Closed machine-local marker variant, JCS identity, exact paths, atomic write, classification, migration, replacement, and crash fixtures in Sections 3.2, 10.6, 11.3, and 11.7 |\n12198|| Anti-entropy namespace membership was partial | Total schema/byte-to-namespace table, local exclusions, mixed-schema roots, and exchange fixture in Section 11.4 |\n12199|| Workspace Group membership had no evolution rule | Immutable topology with membership derived from immutable Session Records and authoritative session Tombstones; exact expectation, concurrent join/leave, and group/worktree takeover rules in Sections 5.6, 11.3, 12.6, and 13.1–13.7 |\n(more lines below)"}}}
