{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000caeb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a076ec-3023-7ad0-af14-c3080467cd16"},"sequence":976,"recorded_at":1780531400001947,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"29de407d-d987-4950-b9b4-211f15150d27","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"29de407d-d987-4950-b9b4-211f15150d27","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"29de407d-d987-4950-b9b4-211f15150d27"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"94faa7ee-4e27-4ea8-ad82-74384f607816"},"task_id":"94faa7ee-4e27-4ea8-ad82-74384f607816","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"94faa7ee-4e27-4ea8-ad82-74384f607816","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-1i3qu7/worktree/internal/dirnode/obligation_census_test.go`.\n1|package dirnode\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"go/ast\"\n5|\t\"os\"\n6|\t\"path/filepath\"\n7|\t\"sort\"\n8|\t\"strconv\"\n9|\t\"strings\"\n10|\t\"testing\"\n11|)\n12|\n13|// This file is the derived query-obligation census (review round\n14|// 3, C2). DecodeQuery reports every operation-level defect through\n15|// the single checkQueryOperation arm, so one witness per arm\n16|// proves the arm exists while thirty-one removable obligations\n17|// hide behind it. The admission half is already derived (the\n18|// seventeen-operation union built from readOperations plus\n19|// mutationOperations, failing closed on a missing builder); this\n20|// file derives the refusal half the same way.\n21|//\n22|// Denominator (deriveQueryObligations): every false-returning site\n23|// in query.go — a bare `return false` or a `return <ZeroLit>,\n24|// false` — keyed query.go|<function>|obligation-<n> by occurrence\n25|// order in its function. That is 112 sites: the reviewer's 89 bare\n26|// sites plus the same-shaped tuple sites in checkCaller (11) and\n27|// checkQueryOperation (12), which hide behind the caller arm and\n28|// the operation arm respectively. Boolean helpers in other files\n29|// funnel into message-distinct arms pinned by the reachability\n30|// gate; query.go is the file whose validators collapse N into one\n31|// message, so it carries its own roster.\n32|//\n33|// Every site carries exactly one row: a vector driven through the\n34|// production DecodeQuery entry that refuses (or, for one\n35|// classification site, admits). Roster fails closed in both\n36|// directions: a derived site with no row fails, and a row naming\n37|// a site production no longer derives fails as orphaned. One site\n38|// is defensive (defensiveObligations) with a structural tripwire,\n39|// not a vector.\n40|//\n41|// Resolution: each refusal vector violates exactly one sibling\n42|// obligation — every other member of its validator holds a valid\n43|// value — so two distinct obligations in one validator cannot both\n44|// satisfy one witness. The committed suite proves each vector\n45|// refuses through the production entry; the attached battery\n46|// proves narrowness by flipping each site alone and recording\n47|// which witnesses fail. Two structural overlaps are stated, not\n48|// hidden:\n49|//\n50|//   - framing gates (checkQueryOperation obligations 7-12):\n51|//     a gate fires exactly when its validator is false, so no\n52|//     vector can violate a gate without violating one obligation\n53|//     beneath it. Gate rows reuse a representative validator\n54|//     witness, documented per row; the battery shows the AND\n55|//     (the witness fails under both flips).\n56|//   - layered delegates (filters arms over checkEnumSubset and\n57|//     checkUUIDv7DigestSubset): a filters witness for a delegated\n58|//     shape necessarily violates the delegate obligation too.\n59|//     Those witnesses name both sites; the battery shows the pair.\n60|\n61|// defensiveObligations names derived sites no public input can\n62|// fire, with the bound that keeps them honest.\n63|var defensiveObligations = map[string]string{\n64|\t// checkQueryParameters obligation-1 fires only when the kind\n65|\t// registry and the parameter-member table disagree on a name:\n66|\t// checkQueryOperation admits only registry names, so through\n67|\t// the production entry the lookup always succeeds while the\n68|\t// tables agree. TestQueryParameterMembersMatchRegistry fails\n69|\t// when the tables diverge, which is exactly when this arm\n70|\t// becomes reachable; a mutant removing it is\n71|\t// behavior-preserving while the tables agree.\n72|\t\"query.go|checkQueryParameters|obligation-1\": \"fires only on registry divergence; pinned by the table-agreement tripwire\",\n73|}\n74|\n75|// deriveQueryObligations derives every false-returning site in\n76|// query.go from production source. A bare `return false` and a\n77|// `return <ZeroLit>, false` both count: both refuse the batch.\n78|// Anything else — expression returns, error returns — is outside\n79|// the obligation shape. An empty derivation fails closed.\n80|func deriveQueryObligations(t *testing.T) map[string]bool {\n81|\tt.Helper()\n82|\tsource, err := readQuerySource(t)\n83|\tif err != nil {\n84|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"obligations: %v\", err)\n85|\t}\n86|\tsyntax, err := parseGoFile(\"query.go\", source)\n87|\tif err != nil {\n88|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"obligations: %v\", err)\n89|\t}\n90|\tsites := map[string]bool{}\n91|\tcounts := map[string]int{}\n92|\tast.Inspect(syntax, func(node ast.Node) bool {\n93|\t\tfunction, ok := node.(*ast.FuncDecl)\n94|\t\tif !ok || function.Body == nil {\n95|\t\t\treturn true\n96|\t\t}\n97|\t\tast.Inspect(function.Body, func(inner ast.Node) bool {\n98|\t\t\treturned, ok := inner.(*ast.ReturnStmt)\n99|\t\t\tif !ok {\n100|\t\t\t\treturn true\n101|\t\t\t}\n102|\t\t\tif len(returned.Results) == 0 {\n103|\t\t\t\treturn true\n104|\t\t\t}\n105|\t\t\tlast, ok := returned.Results[len(returned.Results)-1].(*ast.Ident)\n106|\t\t\tif !ok || last.Name != \"false\" {\n107|\t\t\t\treturn true\n108|\t\t\t}\n109|\t\t\tswitch len(returned.Results) {\n110|\t\t\tcase 1:\n111|\t\t\tcase 2:\n112|\t\t\t\tif _, ok := returned.Results[0].(*ast.CompositeLit); !ok {\n113|\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n114|\t\t\t\t}\n115|\t\t\tdefault:\n116|\t\t\t\treturn true\n117|\t\t\t}\n118|\t\t\tcounts[function.Name.Name]++\n119|\t\t\tsites[singleObligationKey(function.Name.Name, counts[function.Name.Name])] = true\n120|\t\t\treturn true\n121|\t\t})\n122|\t\treturn false\n123|\t})\n124|\tif len(sites) == 0 {\n125|\t\tt.Fatal(\"derived zero query obligations; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n126|\t}\n127|\treturn sites\n128|}\n129|\n130|// readQuerySource reads the production query.go of this package\n131|// directory.\n132|func readQuerySource(t *testing.T) ([]byte, error) {\n133|\tt.Helper()\n134|\tfor _, path := range productionFiles(t) {\n135|\t\tif filepath.Base(path) == \"query.go\" {\n136|\t\t\tcontents, err := os.ReadFile(path)\n137|\t\t\tif err != nil {\n138|\t\t\t\treturn nil, err\n139|\t\t\t}\n140|\t\t\treturn contents, nil\n141|\t\t}\n142|\t}\n143|\tt.Fatal(\"production query.go is not among the scanned files; the census is blind, not complete\")\n144|\treturn nil, nil\n145|}\n146|\n147|// singleObligationKey renders one obligation site key.\n148|func singleObligationKey(function string, ordinal int) string {\n149|\treturn \"query.go|\" + function + \"|obligation-\" + strconv.Itoa(ordinal)\n150|}\n151|\n152|// obligationRow pairs one derived obligation site with the vector\n153|// that exercises it through the production DecodeQuery entry.\n154|// admit marks the single classification row whose vector must be\n155|// admitted rather than refused.\n156|type obligationRow struct {\n157|\tsite  string\n158|\tname  string\n159|\tadmit bool\n160|\tbuild func(t *testing.T) string\n161|}\n162|\n163|// TestQueryObligationRosterIsComplete requires every derived\n164|// query obligation to carry exactly one row (or a defensive\n165|// rationale). It is separate from the behavioral test below on\n166|// purpose: removing a site renumbers its function's ordinals, so\n167|// the roster reddens on any obligation mutant by construction.\n168|// Killer-set analysis reads the behavioral subtests, never this\n169|// roster verdict.\n170|func TestQueryObligationRosterIsComplete(t *testing.T) {\n171|\tt.Parallel()\n172|\tderived := deriveQueryObligations(t)\n173|\trows := obligationRows()\n174|\tseen := map[string]bool{}\n175|\tfor _, row := range rows {\n176|\t\tif !derived[row.site] {\n177|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"orphaned obligation row %q (%s): production derives no such site\", row.site, row.name)\n178|\t\t}\n179|\t\tif seen[row.site] {\n180|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"duplicate obligation row %q: one vector per site keeps the witness narrow\", row.site)\n181|\t\t}\n182|\t\tseen[row.site] = true\n183|\t}\n184|\tvar missing []string\n185|\tfor site := range derived {\n186|\t\tif seen[site] {\n187|\t\t\tcontinue\n188|\t\t}\n189|\t\tif _, defensive := defensiveObligations[site]; defensive {\n190|\t\t\tcontinue\n191|\t\t}\n192|\t\tmissing = append(missing, site)\n193|\t}\n194|\tsort.Strings(missing)\n195|\tif len(missing) > 0 {\n196|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"derived obligations with no witness vector:\\n  %s\", strings.Join(missing, \"\\n  \"))\n197|\t}\n198|}\n199|\n200|// TestEveryQueryObligationIsDriven drives each obligation row's\n201|// vector through the production DecodeQuery entry. A removed\n202|// obligation admits its refusal vector — or, for the admission\n203|// row, refuses it — and fails the named subtest here.\n204|func TestEveryQueryObligationIsDriven(t *testing.T) {\n205|\tt.Parallel()\n206|\trows := obligationRows()\n207|\tfor _, row := range rows {\n208|\t\trow := row\n209|\t\tt.Run(row.site, func(t *testing.T) {\n210|\t\t\tt.Parallel()\n211|\t\t\t_, err := DecodeQuery([]byte(row.build(t)))\n212|\t\t\tif row.admit {\n213|\t\t\t\tif err != nil {\n214|\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"row %q (%s): admission vector refused: %v\", row.site, row.name, err)\n215|\t\t\t\t}\n216|\t\t\t\treturn\n217|\t\t\t}\n218|\t\t\tif failure := requireCode(t, err, \"query_invalid\"); failure == nil {\n219|\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"row %q (%s): refusal vector admitted\", row.site, row.name)\n220|\t\t\t}\n221|\t\t})\n222|\t}\n223|}\n224|\n225|// TestQueryParameterMembersMatchRegistry is the structural\n226|// tripwire for the defensive checkQueryParameters obligation-1:\n227|// the parameter-member table must key exactly the operation\n228|// union. A name the kind registry admits but the member table\n229|// misses would reach the defensive arm; this test fails first.\n230|func TestQueryParameterMembersMatchRegistry(t *testing.T) {\n231|\tt.Parallel()\n232|\tunion := append(append([]string(nil), readOperations...), mutationOperations...)\n233|\tif len(union) != 17 {\n234|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"query union = %d operations, want 17\", len(union))\n235|\t}\n236|\tif len(queryParameterMembers) != len(union) {\n237|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"parameter-member table keys = %d, want the %d union members\", len(queryParameterMembers), len(union))\n238|\t}\n239|\tfor _, name := range union {\n240|\t\tmembers, ok := queryParameterMembers[name]\n241|\t\tif !ok || len(members) == 0 {\n242|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"operation %q has no parameter-member row; the defensive lookup would fire\", name)\n243|\t\t}\n244|\t}\n245|}\n246|\n247|// sessionsWith substitutes one needle inside the valid sessions\n248|// parameters, failing when the needle is absent so the vector\n249|// cannot pass vacuously.\n250|func sessionsWith(t *testing.T, needle, replacement string) string {\n251|\tt.Helper()\n252|\tparams := operationParams(\"sessions\")\n253|\tif !strings.Contains(params, needle) {\n254|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"sessions needle %q absent; the vector mutates nothing\", needle)\n255|\t}\n256|\treturn refuseBatch(\"sessions\", strings.Replace(params, needle, replacement, 1))\n257|}\n258|\n259|// filtersWith substitutes one needle inside the valid filters\n260|// body of the sessions parameters.\n261|func filtersWith(t *testing.T, needle, replacement string) string {\n262|\tt.Helper()\n263|\tif !strings.Contains(validFiltersJSON, needle) {\n264|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"filters needle %q absent; the vector mutates nothing\", needle)\n265|\t}\n266|\treturn sessionsWith(t, needle, replacement)\n267|}\n268|\n269|// callerBatch wraps one caller object in the valid two-operation\n270|// batch, so the refusal is attributable to the caller.\n271|func callerBatch(t *testing.T, caller string) string {\n272|\tt.Helper()\n273|\tgood := fixtureQueryJSON()\n274|\tif !strings.Contains(good, fixtureCallerJSON()) {\n275|\t\tt.Fatal(\"callerBatch: fixture caller absent; the vector mutates nothing\")\n276|\t}\n277|\treturn strings.Replace(good, fixtureCallerJSON(), caller, 1)\n278|}\n279|\n280|// callerWith substitutes one needle inside the valid caller\n281|// object.\n282|func callerWith(t *testing.T, needle, replacement string) string {\n283|\tt.Helper()\n284|\tcaller := fixtureCallerJSON()\n285|\tif !strings.Contains(caller, needle) {\n286|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"caller needle %q absent; the vector mutates nothing\", needle)\n287|\t}\n288|\treturn callerBatch(t, strings.Replace(caller, needle, replacement, 1))\n289|}\n290|\n291|// obligationRows pairs every fireable derived obligation site\n292|// with its narrow vector. Each vector violates exactly the named\n293|// sibling obligation (layered delegates and shared framing gates\n294|// are documented per row); every other member holds a valid\n295|// value.\n296|func obligationRows() []obligationRow {\n297|\treturn []obligationRow{\n298|\t\t{site: \"query.go|isListOperation|obligation-1\", name: \"count with list pagination\", build: func(t *testing.T) string {\n299|\t\t\t// Shared with the pagination-gate row: the gate\n300|\t\t\t// admits list pagination exactly when this\n301|\t\t\t// classification does, so one vector witnesses\n302|\t\t\t// both; the battery shows the AND.\n303|\t\t\treturn singleOperationBatch(\"count\", operationParams(\"count\"), \"null\", \"null\", 0, 10, \"[]\", \"false\", \"false\", \"null\", \"null\")\n304|\t\t}},\n305|\t\t{site: \"query.go|isAnnotationMutation|obligation-1\", name: \"enrich confirmed without expectation admits\", admit: true, build: func(t *testing.T) string {\n306|\t\t\t// Removing the classification admits nothing new\n307|\t\t\t// here: it reroutes enrich into the annotation\n308|\t\t\t// branch, which refuses a confirmed mutation\n309|\t\t\t// without expectation and idempotency digests.\n310|\t\t\treturn mutationBatch(\"enrich\", operationParams(\"enrich\"), false, true, \"null\", \"null\")\n311|\t\t}},\n312|\t\t{site: \"query.go|validQueryField|obligation-1\", name: \"unknown projection field\", build: func(t *testing.T) string {\n313|\t\t\treturn singleOperationBatch(\"sessions\", operationParams(\"sessions\"), `[\"id\",\"nope\"]`, \"null\", 0, 10, \"[]\", \"false\", \"false\", \"null\", \"null\")\n314|\t\t}},\n315|\t\t{site: \"query.go|validQueryPreset|obligation-1\", name: \"unknown preset\", build: func(t *testing.T) string {\n316|\t\t\treturn singleOperationBatch(\"sessions\", operationParams(\"sessions\"), \"null\", `\"everything\"`, 0, 10, \"[]\", \"false\", \"false\", \"null\", \"null\")\n317|\t\t}},\n318|\t\t{site: \"query.go|checkCaller|obligation-1\", name: \"caller non-object\", build: func(t *testing.T) string {\n319|\t\t\tgood := fixtureQueryJSON()\n320|\t\t\treturn strings.Replace(good, fixtureCallerJSON(), `[]`, 1)\n321|\t\t}},\n322|\t\t{site: \"query.go|checkCaller|obligation-2\", name: \"caller unknown member\", build: func(t *testing.T) string {\n323|\t\t\treturn callerWith(t, `\"extensions\":{}}`, `\"extensions\":{},\"extra\":1}`)\n324|\t\t}},\n325|\t\t{site: \"query.go|checkCaller|obligation-3\", name: \"caller missing member\", build: func(t *testing.T) string {\n326|\t\t\treturn callerWith(t, `\"caller_id\":\"test-caller\",`, ``)\n327|\t\t}},\n328|\t\t{site: \"query.go|checkCaller|obligation-4\", name: \"caller empty identifier\", build: func(t *testing.T) string {\n329|\t\t\treturn callerWith(t, `\"caller_id\":\"test-caller\"`, `\"caller_id\":\"\"`)\n330|\t\t}},\n331|\t\t{site: \"query.go|checkCaller|obligation-5\", name: \"caller empty subject\", build: func(t *testing.T) string {\n332|\t\t\treturn callerWith(t, `\"authentication_subject\":\"test-subject\"`, `\"authentication_subject\":\"\"`)\n333|\t\t}},\n334|\t\t{site: \"query.go|checkCaller|obligation-6\", name: \"caller bad origin host\", build: func(t *testing.T) string {\n335|\t\t\treturn callerWith(t, fixtureOriginHost, \"not-a-uuid\")\n336|\t\t}},\n337|\t\t{site: \"query.go|checkCaller|obligation-7\", name: \"caller bad interaction\", build: func(t *testing.T) string {\n338|\t\t\treturn callerWith(t, `\"non_interactive\"`, `\"whenever\"`)\n339|\t\t}},\n340|\t\t{site: \"query.go|checkCaller|obligation-8\", name: \"caller empty scopes\", build: func(t *testing.T) string {\n341|\t\t\treturn callerWith(t, `\"scopes\":[\"directory.read\"]`, `\"scopes\":[]`)\n342|\t\t}},\n343|\t\t{site: \"query.go|checkCaller|obligation-9\", name: \"caller bad scope\", build: func(t *testing.T) string {\n344|\t\t\treturn callerWith(t, `\"directory.read\"`, `\"directory.root\"`)\n345|\t\t}},\n346|\t\t{site: \"query.go|checkCaller|obligation-10\", name: \"caller bad policy digest\", build: func(t *testing.T) string {\n347|\t\t\treturn callerWith(t, fixturePolicyDigest, \"sha256:zzz\")\n348|\t\t}},\n349|\t\t{site: \"query.go|checkCaller|obligation-11\", name: \"caller bad extensions\", build: func(t *testing.T) string {\n350|\t\t\treturn callerWith(t, `\"extensions\":{}}`, `\"extensions\":{\"x\":1}}`)\n351|\t\t}},\n352|\t\t{site: \"query.go|checkQueryOperation|obligation-1\", name: \"operation non-object element\", build: func(t *testing.T) string {\n353|\t\t\tschema := queryOperationJSON(0, \"schema\", `{\"extensions\":{}}`, \"null\", \"null\", 0, 1, \"[]\", \"false\", \"false\", \"null\", \"null\")\n354|\t\t\treturn `{\"schema\":\"urn:ax:schema:session-directory-query\",\"schema_version\":\"1.0.0\",\"query_id\":` + quote(fixtureQueryID) + `,\"operations\":[` + schema + `,[]],\"caller\":` + fixtureCallerJSON() + `,\"extensions\":{}}`\n355|\t\t}},\n356|\t\t{site: \"query.go|checkQueryOperation|obligation-2\", name: \"operation unknown member\", build: func(t *testing.T) string {\n357|\t\t\tbatch := singleOperationBatch(\"sessions\", operationParams(\"sessions\"), \"null\", `\"overview\"`, 0, 10, \"[]\", \"false\", \"false\", \"null\", \"null\")\n358|\t\t\treturn strings.Replace(batch, `\"preset\":\"overview\"`, `\"preset\":\"overview\",\"extra\":1`, 1)\n359|\t\t}},\n360|\t\t{site: \"query.go|checkQueryOperation|obligation-3\", name: \"operation missing member\", build: func(t *testing.T) string {\n361|\t\t\tbatch := operationBatch(\"sessions\")\n362|\t\t\tif !strings.Contains(batch, `\"take\":10,`) {\n363|\t\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"take needle absent; the vector mutates nothing\")\n364|\t\t\t}\n365|\t\t\treturn strings.Replace(batch, `\"take\":10,`, ``, 1)\n366|\t\t}},\n367|\t\t{site: \"query.go|checkQueryOperation|obligation-4\", name: \"operation duplicate index\", build: func(t *testing.T) string {\n368|\t\t\treturn strings.Replace(fixtureQueryJSON(), `\"operation_index\":1`, `\"operation_index\":0`, 1)\n369|\t\t}},\n370|\t\t{site: \"query.go|checkQueryOperation|obligation-5\", name: \"operation non-string name\", build: func(t *testing.T) string {\n371|\t\t\tbatch := operationBatch(\"sessions\")\n372|\t\t\treturn strings.Replace(batch, `\"name\":\"sessions\"`, `\"name\":0`, 1)\n373|\t\t}},\n374|\t\t{site: \"query.go|checkQueryOperation|obligation-6\", name: \"operation unknown name\", build: func(t *testing.T) string {\n375|\t\t\tbatch := operationBatch(\"sessions\")\n376|\t\t\treturn strings.Replace(batch, `\"name\":\"sessions\"`, `\"name\":\"search\"`, 1)\n377|\t\t}},\n378|\t\t{site: \"query.go|checkQueryOperation|obligation-7\", name: \"parameters gate shares the schema-extra witness\", build: func(t *testing.T) string {\n379|\t\t\t// Framing gate over the parameter union: no vector\n380|\t\t\t// violates the gate without violating one\n381|\t\t\t// obligation beneath it, so the row reuses that\n382|\t\t\t// obligation's witness. The battery shows the AND:\n383|\t\t\t// the witness fails under both flips.\n384|\t\t\treturn refuseBatch(\"schema\", `{\"extensions\":{},\"extra\":1}`)\n385|\t\t}},\n386|\t\t{site: \"query.go|checkQueryOperation|obligation-8\", name: \"projection gate shares the fields-and-preset witness\", build: func(t *testing.T) string {\n387|\t\t\treturn singleOperationBatch(\"sessions\", operationParams(\"sessions\"), `[\"id\"]`, `\"overview\"`, 0, 10, \"[]\", \"false\", \"false\", \"null\", \"null\")\n388|\t\t}},\n389|\t\t{site: \"query.go|checkQueryOperation|obligation-9\", name: \"pagination gate shares the count-take witness\", build: func(t *testing.T) string {\n390|\t\t\treturn singleOperationBatch(\"count\", operationParams(\"count\"), \"null\", \"null\", 0, 10, \"[]\", \"false\", \"false\", \"null\", \"null\")\n391|\t\t}},\n392|\t\t{site: \"query.go|checkQueryOperation|obligation-10\", name: \"sort gate shares the unknown-sort-field witness\", build: func(t *testing.T) string {\n393|\t\t\treturn singleOperationBatch(\"sessions\", operationParams(\"sessions\"), \"null\", \"null\", 0, 10, `[{\"field\":\"vibes\",\"direction\":\"asc\",\"extensions\":{}}]`, \"false\", \"false\", \"null\", \"null\")\n394|\t\t}},\n395|\t\t{site: \"query.go|checkQueryOperation|obligation-11\", name: \"flags gate shares the unconfirmed-execute-plan witness\", build: func(t *testing.T) string {\n396|\t\t\treturn mutationBatch(\"execute_plan\", operationParams(\"execute_plan\"), true, false, \"null\", \"null\")\n397|\t\t}},\n398|\t\t{site: \"query.go|checkQueryOperation|obligation-12\", name: \"operation extensions gate\", build: func(t *testing.T) string {\n399|\t\t\tbatch := operationBatch(\"sessions\")\n400|\t\t\treturn strings.Replace(batch, `\"idempotency_key\":null,\"extensions\":{}}]`, `\"idempotency_key\":null,\"extensions\":{