eck -section 6.2\\n383:[`internal/provider`](internal/provider) implements the Section 7.1 trusted\\n414:go test ./internal/provider -count=1\\n415:go test ./internal/provider -cover -count=1\\n422:against the digest-pinned document in `internal/specdoc`, quoting the exact\\n427:[`internal/provhost`](internal/provhost) implements the ax host side of\\n488:go test ./internal/provhost -count=1\\n489:go test ./internal/provhost -cover -count=1\\n506:arm, so a planted arm or a deleted branch reddens in either direction. This inventory is independent of the per-package refusal inventories in [`internal/provider`](internal/provider) above and [`internal/terminalbackend`](internal/terminalbackend) below (see [Specification-to-Code Ownership Gate](#specification-to-code-ownership-gate)): each package derives its own refusal arms from its own source in its own test file, and the three share no inventory code or table.\\n513:[`internal/canonicaljson`](internal/canonicaljson) exposes the production RFC\\n591:[`internal/canonicaljson/testdata/constraint-enumeration.md`](internal/canonicaljson/testdata/constraint-enumeration.md).\\n599:[`internal/specdoc`](internal/specdoc) document verbatim, beginning on the exact\\n776:graph, and against the digest-pinned document in `internal/specdoc` — a quoted\\n818:[`testdata/closed-vocabularies.md`](internal/canonicaljson/testdata/closed-vocabularies.md).\\n834:[`internal/specdoc`](internal/specdoc) does not yet gate them. Admitting an extra member, dropping one, reordering\\n915:the production `internal/scalar` parsers rather than by member name. The fixture\\n993:[`testdata/array-order-constraints.md`](internal/canonicaljson/testdata/array-order-constraints.md).\\n1038:[`record_conformance_test.go`](internal/canonicaljson/record_conformance_test.go).\\n1149:go test ./internal/canonicaljson -count=1\\n1150:go test ./internal/canonicaljson -cover -count=1\\n1151:go test ./internal/canonicaljson -run=^$ \\\\\\n1153:go test ./internal/canonicaljson -run=^$ \\\\\\n1155:go test ./internal/canonicaljson -run=^$ \\\\\\n1157:go test ./internal/canonicaljson -run=^$ \\\\\\n1159:go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 3139,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 785,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
